Problems Found During Testing

Description
This document contains a list of founded issues during testing.
The final decision on whether it is a bug or a feature should be made after reviewing the technical requirements.

 --- Create Player ---

 Issue 1:
    name:           Player is created with GET request instead of POST.
    Steps:          1. Send a GET request to create a player.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system creates a player with a GET request.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that the method is not allowed.

 Issue 2:
    name:           After creating a player, the system returns only "id" and "login" fields instead of full player information.
    Steps:          Make any request which creates a new Player e.g.
                    GET http://3.68.165.45/player/create/supervisor?password=34k3XehL0iiF&role=admin&gender=female&screenName=S5sLye72UT&login=UiBV7RRn&age=44

                    Actual: The system return response with code 200 and the following fields:
                    {
                        "id":166644577,
                        "login":"UiBV7RRn",
                        "password":null,
                        "screenName":null,
                        "gender":null,
                        "age":null,
                        "role":null
                    }
                    Expected: all fields are filled out with sent parameters

 Issue 3:
     name:          The system updates the player's information through the create player request.
     Steps:
                    1. Create a player with login "test".
                    2. Update the player model except the login field.
                    3. Send a request to create a player with the same login.
                    Actual: The system updated already created player with the same login.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that login is already taken.

Issue 4:
     name:          Password field is not mandatory during player creation via GET request.
     Steps:
                    1. Send a request to create a player without password parameter.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system creates a player without password.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that password is required.

--- Delete Player ---

Issue 5:
    name:           The system allows to delete a player with admin editor role.
    Precondition:   The player is available for deleting present in the system.
    Steps:          1. Send a request to delete a player as admin editor.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system deletes a player without checking the role of the editor.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that the editor does not have permission to delete a player.

Issue 6:
    name:          The system returns 403 status code instead of 404 after sending a request to delete a non-existent player.
    Steps:         1. Send a request to delete a player with a non-existent id.
                   2. Check the response.
                   Actual: The system returns 403 status code.
                   Expected: The system should return 404 status code.

--- Get Player ---

Issue 7:
    name:           The POST request is used to get player information.
    Steps:          1. Send a POST request to get player information.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns player information with a POST request.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that the method is not allowed.

Issue 8:
    name:           The system returns 200 status code instead of 404 after sending a request to get information about a non-existent player.
    Steps:          1. Send a request to get information about a player with a non-existent id.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns 200 status code.
                    Expected: The system should return 404 status code.

Issue 9:
    name:           200 status code returns after a request with wrong schema validation for the get player request
    Steps:          1. Send a request to get player information with body e.g.
                    {
                     "test": "test"
                    }
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns status code 200.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that the schema is not valid.

Issue 10:
    name:           Periodically the system returns the response with the delay of 10 seconds.
    Steps:          1. Send a request to get player information.
                    2. Check the response time.
                    Actual: The system returns the response with a delay of 10 seconds.
                    Expected: The system should return the response without a delay.
                    Note: The issue is not stable and appears periodically.

--- Get all Players ---

Issue 11:
    name:           Role field of the player is not present in the response after sending a request to get all players.
    Steps:          1. Send a request to get all players.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns a response without the role field.
                    Expected: According to swagger documentation the system should return a response with the role field.

--- Update Player ---

Issue 12:
    name:           200 status code returns after a request with wrong schema validation for the get player request
    Steps:          1. Send a request to get player information with body e.g.
                    {
                     "test": "test"
                    }
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns status code 200.
                    Expected: The system should return an error message that the schema is not valid.

Issue 13:
    name:           The role of the player is not updated after sending a request to update the player.
    Steps:          1. Send a request to update the player role.
                    PATCH http://3.68.165.45/player/update/supervisor/19345674
                    {
                          "role": "admin"
                    }
                    2. Check the response.
                    {
                          "id": 19345674,
                          "login": "OUyo445ssl",
                          "screenName": "yKmFFola466",
                          "gender": "male",
                          "age": 60,
                          "role": "user"
                    }
                    Actual: The system returns a response with the updated role.
                    Expected: The system should return a response with the updated role.

--- General ---

Issue 13:
    name:           Periodically the backend returns 403 error status code on any request.
    Steps:          1. Send a valid request to the backend.
                    2. Check the response.
                    Actual: The system returns 403 status code.
                    Expected: The system should return a valid response.